load 0
=== mmseqs
--- mmseqs 
createdb 	convert FASTA/Q file(s) to a sequence DB
easy-cluster 	slower, sensitive clustering
easy-search 	sensitive homology search
--- mmseqs easy-
easy-cluster 	slower, sensitive clustering
easy-search 	sensitive homology search
--- mmseqs createdb -
--dbtype=	database type 0: auto, 1: amino acid 2: nucleotides
--local-tmp=	path where some of the temporary files will be created
--mask=	mask sequences in prefilter stage with tantan: 0: w/o low complexity masking, 1: with low complexity masking
--shuffle=	shuffle input database
--threads=	number of CPU-cores used (all by default)
-v 	verbosity level: 0: quiet, 1: +errors, 2: +warnings, 3: +info
--- mmseqs createdb --shuffle 
0 
1 
--- mmseqs createdb --dbtype 
--- mmseqs createdb --local-tmp 
--- mmseqs createdb my
mydb.fa 
--- mmseqs easy-search -e
-e 	list matches below this E-value (range 0.0-inf)
--- mmseqs easy-search --add-self-matches 
0 
1 
--- mmseqs nosuchmodule --
--- mmseqs ../evil --
